{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftLLM"}],"role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Native Metal MSL Shaders for Quantized LLMs"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/TransformerDecoderArchitecture","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/WeightParsingAndSampling"],"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials","generated":true,"title":"Guides & Tutorials"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"article","sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftllm\/metalshadersquantization"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM"]]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Quantization--Metal-Execution","title":"Quantization & Metal Execution","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizedLinear","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizationScheme","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalQuantizedEngine","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalQuantizedError"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Large language models like Llama 3, Mistral, and DeepSeek require massive memory bandwidth. Weight-only quantization (such as GGUF Q4_0 and Q8_0) compresses 16-bit floating-point weights into 4-bit or 8-bit integer blocks with group scaling factors, reducing memory footprint by 50% to 75%."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftLLM"},{"type":"text","text":" implements native Metal Shading Language (MSL) SIMD kernels executing hardware dequantization and GEMV \/ GEMM transformations directly on Apple Silicon GPUs without intermediate CPU memory allocations."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Architecture","text":"Architecture"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["Packed Quantized Weights [Q4_0 \/ Q8_0]   Scale Factors [FP16]   Input Activations [FP32]","                 │                               │                        │","                 └───────────────────────┬───────┴────────────────────────┘","                                         ▼","                   Metal Compute Command Encoder","                                         │","                 ┌───────────────────────┴───────────────────────┐","                 ▼                                               ▼","     MSL Kernel: gemv_q4_0                           MSL Kernel: gemv_q8_0","   - Unpack 4-bit nibbles (w - 8)                  - Load signed 8-bit integers","   - Multiply by group FP16 scale                  - Multiply by group FP16 scale","   - Accumulate with input vector                  - Accumulate with input vector","                 │                                               │","                 └───────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘","                                         ▼","                            Output Activation Vector","                               (Unified Memory)"],"syntax":null},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"SIMD-Group Matrix Multiplication","anchor":"SIMD-Group-Matrix-Multiplication"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On Apple Silicon (M-series GPUs), threads within a 32-thread SIMD-group collaborate on 8x8 matrix tiles using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"metal_simdgroup_matrix"},{"type":"text","text":". This eliminates thread divergence and ensures maximal utilization of the GPU arithmetic units:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["#include <metal_stdlib>","#include <metal_simdgroup_matrix>","","using namespace metal;","","kernel void gemm_simdgroup_q4_0(","    device const half* A               [[buffer(0)]],","    device const half* B               [[buffer(1)]],","    device half* C                     [[buffer(2)]],","    constant uint& M                   [[buffer(3)]],","    constant uint& N                   [[buffer(4)]],","    constant uint& K                   [[buffer(5)]],","    uint2 threadgroup_position_in_grid [[threadgroup_position_in_grid]],","    uint simdgroup_index_in_threadgroup [[simdgroup_index_in_threadgroup]]",") {","    simdgroup_matrix<half, 8, 8> acc;","    acc = make_filled_simdgroup_matrix<half, 8, 8>(0.0h);","    \/\/ Accumulate across inner K dimension...","}"],"syntax":"metal"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Swift-API-Integration","text":"Swift API Integration"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"QuantizedLinear","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" exposes both MLX tensor inference and direct Metal kernel execution:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftLLM","","\/\/ 1. Create a quantized linear layer (e.g. 4096 in, 4096 out)","let linear = QuantizedLinear(","    inFeatures: 4096,","    outFeatures: 4096,","    scheme: .q4_0,","    weight: mlxWeights,","    scales: mlxScales",")","","\/\/ 2. Direct Metal shader execution without CPU round-trips","let outputs = try linear.forwardMetal(","    inVector: inputActivations,","    rawWeights: packedQ4Bytes,","    rawScales: fp16Scales",")"],"syntax":"swift"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Hardware dequantization and SIMD-group matrix multiplication for 4-bit and 8-bit quantized weights on Apple Silicon GPU."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalShadersQuantization"},"references":{"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Local Causal Transformer Decoder & Weight Parsers."}],"role":"collection","title":"SwiftLLM","url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm"},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/MetalQuantizedError":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalQuantizedError","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"